33\\t\\n  3534\\t    (and (map? pre) (:type pre) (map? stamped) (:type stamped))\\n  3535\\t    (do (when (not= (:type pre) (:type stamped))\\n  3536\\t          (throw (ex-info \\\"Stamped tree diverges from the compiled tree\\\"\\n  3537\\t                          {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\\n  3538\\t                           :pre-stamp-path pre-path\\n  3539\\t                           :stamped-path stamped-path\\n  3540\\t                           :pre-type (:type pre)\\n  3541\\t                           :stamped-type (:type stamped)})))\\n  3542\\t        (reduce (fn [acc [j [field kind]]]\\n  3543\\t                  (let [pos (+ j 2)\\n  3544\\t                        pv (get pre field)\\n  3545\\t                        sv (get stamped field)]\\n  3546\\t                    (case kind\\n  3547\\t                      :node (if (or (map? pv) (map? sv))\\n  3548\\t                              (cc3-correspond pv sv\\n  3549\\t                                              (conj pre-path pos)\\n  3550\\t                                              (conj stamped-path pos)\\n  3551\\t                                              acc)\\n  3552\\t                              acc)\\n  3553\\t                      :nodes (do (when (not= (count (or pv []))\\n  3554\\t                                             (count (or sv [])))\\n  3555\\t                                   (throw (ex-info\\n  3556\\t                                            \\\"Stamped tree diverges from the compiled tree\\\"\\n  3557\\t                                            {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\\n  3558\\t                                             :pre-stamp-path pre-path\\n  3559\\t                                             :stamped-path stamped-path})))\\n  3560\\t                                 (reduce (fn [a i]\\n  3561\\t                                           (cc3-correspond (nth pv i)\\n  3562\\t                                                           (nth sv i)\\n  3563\\t                                                           (conj pre-path [pos i])\\n  3564\\t                                                           (conj stamped-path [pos i])\\n  3565\\t                                                           a))\\n  3566\\t                                         acc\\n  3567\\t                                         (range (count (or pv [])))))\\n  3568\\t                      ;; scalar grammar data (:data/:sym/:syms/:bool/\\n  3569\\t                      ;; :kw/:key/:str/:int) must be unchanged at the\\n  3570\\t                      ;; translated position — a same-shape mutation\\n  3571\\t                      ;; (callee name, literal value, lambda params)\\n  3572\\t                      ;; is no correspondence (r3 F1)\\n  3573\\t                      (if (= pv sv)\\n  3574\\t                        acc\\n  3575\\t                        (throw (ex-info\\n  3576\\t                                 \\\"Stamped tree diverges from the compiled tree\\\"\\n  3577\\t                                 {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\\n  3578\\t                                  :pre-stamp-path pre-path\\n  3579\\t                                  :stamped-path stamped-path\\n  3580\\t                                  :field field\\n  3581\\t                                  :pre-value pv\\n  3582\\t                                  :stamped-value sv}))))))\\n  3583\\t                (assoc acc stamped-path pre-path)\\n  3584\\t                (map-indexed vector\\n  3585\\t                             (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar\\n  3586\\t                                  (:type pre)))))\\n  3587\\t\\n  3588\\t    (or (map? pre) (map? stamped))\\n  3589\\t    (throw (ex-info \\\"Stamped tree diverges from the compiled tree\\\"\\n  3590\\t                    {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\\n  3591\\t                     :pre-stamp-path pre-path\\n  3592\\t                     :stamped-path stamped-path}))\\n  3593\\t\\n  3594\\t    :else (if (= pre stamped)\\n  3595\\t            acc\\n  3596\\t            (throw (ex-info \\\"Stamped tree diverges from the compiled tree\\\"\\n  3597\\t                            {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\\n  3598\\t                             :pre-stamp-path pre-path\\n  3599\\t                             :stamped-path stamped-path\\n  3600\\t                             :pre-value pre\\n  3601\\t                             :stamped-value stamped})))))\\n  3602\\t\\n  3603\\t\\n  3604\\t(defn- cc3-oracle-binding\\n  3605\\t  \\\"Bind each stamped oracle site id to its post-expansion C1 key\\n  3606\\t   K = [origin root path] in the COMPILED (pre-stamp) tree.\\n  3607\\t\\n  3608\\t   Chronology (mob condition 2): `kernel-compile` compiles FIRST and\\n  3609\\t   stamps by insertion afterward, so the stamped tree is a NEW tree.\\n  3610\\t   Stamped paths are NOT pre-stamp paths (cc3 r2 item 1): the binding\\n  3611\\t   translates each stamped site path through the explicit\\n  3612\\t   `cc3-correspond` transformation mapping before combining it with\\n  3613\\t   the pre-stamp root, and refuses a site whose mapped key is no\\n  3614\\t   validated C1 occurrence. The origin is the admission coordinate\\n  3615\\t   `kernel-compile` recorded WHEN ADMITTING the fixture and retained\\n  3616\\t   with the compilation (`:admission-origin`, cc3 r2 item 2) — never\\n  3617\\t   synthesized from content after compilation; a compilation without\\n  3618\\t   a retained record refuses with `:rule :cc3-admission-record`, and\\n  3619\\t   [:oracle/fixture <id>] is never minted.\\\"\\n  3620\\t  [compiled]\\n  3621\\t  (let [admission (:admission-origin compiled)]\\n  3622\\t    (when-not (vm/occurrence-origin? admission)\\n  3623\\t      (throw (ex-info \\\"Oracle binding requires the compilation's retained admission record\\\"\\n  3624\\t                      {:rule :cc3-admission-record\\n  3625\\t                       :admission admission})))\\n  3626\\t    (let [ast (:compiled-ast compiled)\\n  3627\\t          token (nth admission 2)\\n  3628\\t          origin admission\\n  3629\\t          projected (fn [tree-ast]\\n  3630\\t                      (encoder/project\\n  3631\\t                        (encoder/source-envelope :program token [tree-ast])))\\n  3632\\t          {:keys [tree rows marked eligible]}\\n  3633\\t          (let [p (projected ast)\\n  3634\\t                t (first (:yin/batch p))\\n  3635\\t                r (:yin/frontend-metadata p)]\\n  3636\\t            {:tree t :rows r\\n  3637\\t             :marked (into #{}\\n  3638\\t                           (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\\n  3639\\t                                 (map (fn [[o rr pth _ _]] [o rr pth])))\\n  3640\\t                           r)\\n  3641\\t             :eligible (into #{}\\n  3642\\t                             (map (fn [[rr pth]] [origin rr pth]))\\n  3643\\t                             (vm/application-occurrences t))})\\n  3644\\t          ;; the POST-transformation tree verified separately (item 5)\\n  3645\\t          {:keys [stamped-tree stamped-rows stamped-marked stamped-eligible]}\\n  3646\\t          (let [p (projected (:ast compiled))\\n  3647\\t                t (first (:yin/batch p))\\n  3648\\t                r (:yin/frontend-metadata p)]\\n  3649\\t            {:stamped-tree t :stamped-rows r\\n  3650\\t             :stamped-marked (into #{}\\n  3651\\t                                   (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\\n  3652\\t                                         (map (fn [[o rr pth _ _]] [o rr pth])))\\n  3653\\t                                   r)\\n  3654\\t             :stamped-eligible (into #{}\\n  3655\\t                                     (map (fn [[rr pth]] [origin rr pth]))\\n  3656\\t                                     (vm/application-occurrences t))})\\n  3657\\t          correspondence (cc3-correspond ast (:ast compiled) [] [] {})\\n  3658\\t          ;; site entries are collected BEFORE any map is built: a\\n  3659\\t          ;; duplicate site id refuses here, never overwrites an\\n  3660\\t          ;; earlier occurrence in a map under construction (r3 F1)\\n  3661\\t          site-entries (into []\\n  3662\\t                             (comp (filter (fn [[_ node]]\\n  3663\\t                                             (= :application (:type node))))\\n  3664\\t                                   (keep (fn [[path node]]\\n  3665\\t                                           (let [direct (cc3-stamp-site-id\\n  3666\\t                                                          (second (:operands node)))\\n  3667\\t                                                 inner (kernel-routed-call? node)\\n  3668\\t                                                 routed (when inner\\n  3669\\t                                                          (cc3-stamp-site-id\\n  3670\\t                                                            (first (:operands inner))))]\\n  3671\\t                                             (when-let [k (or direct routed)]\\n  3672\\t                                               (let [pre-path (get correspondence\\n  3673\\t                                                                   path\\n  3674\\t                                                                   ::unmapped)]\\n  3675\\t                                                 (when (= ::unmapped pre-path)\\n  3676\\t                                                   (throw (ex-info\\n  3677\\t                                                            \\\"Stamped site has no pre-stamp correspondence\\\"\\n  3678\\t                                                            {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\\n  3679\\t                                                             :site k\\n  3680\\t                                                             :stamped-path path})))\\n  3681\\t                                                 (let [key [origin (:root tree) pre-path]]\\n  3682\\t                                                   (when-not (contains? marked key)\\n  3683\\t                                                     (throw (ex-info\\n  3684\\t                                                              \\\"Stamped site maps to no validated C1 occurrence\\\"\\n  3685\\t                                                              {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\\n  3686\\t                                                               :site k\\n  3687\\t                                                               :key key})))\\n  3688\\t                                                   [k path key])))))))\\n  3689\\t                             (cc3-walk (:ast compiled) [] []))\\n  3690\\t          _ (when (not= (count site-entries)\\n  3691\\t                        (count (into #{} (map first site-entries))))\\n  3692\\t              (throw (ex-info \\\"Duplicate stamped site id\\\"\\n  3693\\t                              {:rule :cc3-duplicate-stamp-site\\n  3694\\t                               :sites (vec (sort (into []\\n  3695\\t                                                       (comp (filter (fn [[_ n]]\\n  3696\\t                                                                       (< 1 n)))\\n  3697\\t                                                             (map first))\\n  3698\\t                                                       (frequencies\\n  3699\\t                                                         (map first\\n  3700\\t                                                              site-entries)))))})))\\n  3701\\t          stamped-paths (into {}\\n  3702\\t                              (map (fn [[k path _key]] [k path]))\\n  3703\\t                              site-entries)\\n  3704\\t          stamped-sites (into {}\\n  3705\\t                              (map (fn [[k _path key]] [k key]))\\n  3706\\t                              site-entries)]\\n  3707\\t      (when (not= (count stamped-sites)\\n  3708\\t                  (count (into #{} (vals stamped-sites))))\\n  3709\\t        (throw (ex-info \\\"Two stamped sites map to one pre-stamp occurrence\\\"\\n  3710\\t                        {:rule :cc3-ambiguous-stamp-correspondence\\n  3711\\t                         :binding stamped-sites})))\\n  3712\\t      {:origin origin :tree tree :rows rows :marked marked\\n  3713\\t       :eligible eligible :binding stamped-sites\\n  3714\\t       :correspondence correspondence\\n  3715\\t       :stamped-paths stamped-paths\\n  3716\\t       :stamped-tree stamped-tree :stamped-rows stamped-rows\\n  3717\\t       :stamped-marked stamped-marked\\n  3718\\t       :stamped-eligible stamped-eligible})))\\n  3719\\t\\n  3720\\t\\n  3904\\t(deftest test-cc3-correspondence-verifies-grammar-data\\n  3905\\t  ;; cc3 r3 item F1: correspondence must verify scalar grammar data at\\n  3906\\t  ;; translated positions, the wrapper recognizer must verify the\\n  3907\\t  ;; helper is gate-site!, and duplicate site ids must refuse before\\n  3908\\t  ;; any site map is constructed.\\n  3909\\t  (let [lit (fn [v] {:type :literal :value v})\\n  3910\\t        var* (fn [n] {:type :variable :name n})\\n  3911\\t        app (fn [op ops] {:type :application :operator op :operands ops})\\n  3912\\t        intra (fn [f args] (app (var* 'dsg__intra_call) [(var* f) args]))\\n  3913\\t        conj-args (fn [& xs] (app (var* 'conj) (into [(lit [])] xs)))\\n  3914\\t        inner (intra 'f (conj-args (lit 41)))\\n  3915\\t        outer (intra 'g (conj-args inner (lit 7)))\\n  3916\\t        {stamped :ast} (kernel-stamp-sites outer #{'f 'g})\\n  3917\\t        refusal (fn [pre stamped-tree]\\n  3918\\t                  (try (cc3-correspond pre stamped-tree [] [] {})\\n  3919\\t                       ::no-failure\\n  3920\\t                       (catch Exception e (:rule (ex-data e)))))]\\n  3921\\t    (testing \\\"same-shape scalar mutations refuse\\\"\\n  3922\\t      (is (= :cc3-stamp-correspondence\\n  3923\\t             (refusal (var* 'f) (var* 'h)))\\n  3924\\t          \\\"a changed callee variable name preserves shape but not grammar data\\\")\\n  3925\\t      (is (= :cc3-stamp-correspondence\\n  3926\\t             (refusal (lit 41) (lit 42)))\\n  3927\\t          \\\"a changed literal value preserves shape but not grammar data\\\")\\n  3928\\t      (is (= :cc3-stamp-correspondence\\n  3929\\t             (refusal {:type :lambda :params '[x] :body (lit 1)}\\n  3930\\t                      {:type :lambda :params '[y] :body (lit 1)}))\\n  3931\\t          \\\"changed lambda parameters preserve shape but not grammar data\\\")\\n  3932\\t      (let [entries (cc3-walk stamped [] [])\\n  3933\\t            callee-path (some (fn [[p node]]\\n  3934\\t                                (when (and (= :application (:type node))\\n  3935\\t                                           (= 'f (get-in node [:operands 0 :name])))\\n  3936\\t                                  p))\\n  3937\\t                              entries)\\n  3938\\t            mutated (cc3-assoc-at stamped callee-path\\n  3939\\t                                   (fn [node]\\n  3940\\t                                     (assoc-in node [:operands 0 :name] 'h)))]\\n  3941\\t        (is (some? callee-path))\\n  3942\\t        (is (= :cc3-stamp-correspondence (refusal outer mutated))\\n  3943\\t            \\\"a renamed nested callee refuses through the stamped tree\\\")))\\n  3944\\t    (testing \\\"the wrapper recognizer verifies the gate-site! helper\\\"\\n  3945\\t      (let [wrapper (some (fn [[_ node]]\\n  3946\\t                            (when (kernel-stamped-args? node) node))\\n  3947\\t                          (cc3-walk stamped [] []))\\n  3948\\t            mutated (assoc-in wrapper [:operands 0 :operands 0 :name]\\n  3949\\t                              'not-gate-site!)]\\n  3950\\t        (is (some? wrapper) \\\"precondition: a real stamping wrapper exists\\\")\\n  3951\\t        (is (nil? (kernel-stamped-args? mutated))\\n  3952\\t            \\\"a 3-arg application around another helper is no wrapper\\\")\\n  3953\\t        (is (= :cc3-stamp-correspondence (refusal outer\\n  3954\\t                                                  (cc3-assoc-at\\n  3955\\t                                                    stamped\\n  3956\\t                                                    (some (fn [[p node]]\\n  3957\\t                                                            (when (identical? node wrapper) p))\\n  3958\\t                                                          (cc3-walk stamped [] []))\\n  3959\\t                                                    (fn [_] mutated))))\\n  3960\\t            \\\"correspondence refuses when the wrapper helper is not gate-site!\\\")))\\n  3961\\t    (testing \\\"duplicate site ids refuse before map construction\\\"\\n  3962\\t      (let [fixture {:id :cc3-binding\\n  3963\\t                     :call '(latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}\\n  3964\\t            compiled (kernel-compile fixture)\\n  3965\\t            wrappers (into []\\n  3966\\t                           (filter (fn [[_ node]]\\n  3967\\t                                     (kernel-stamped-args? node)))\\n  3968\\t                           (cc3-walk (:ast compiled) [] []))\\n  3969\\t            [p2 _] (second wrappers)\\n  3970\\t            k (cc3-stamp-site-id (second (first wrappers)))\\n  3971\\t            duplicated (cc3-assoc-at (:ast compiled) p2\\n  3972\\t                                      (fn [w]\\n  3973\\t                                        (assoc-in w [:operands 0 :operands 1\\n  3974\\t                                                     :operands 1 :value]\\n  3975\\t                                                  k)))]\\n  3976\\t        (is (= :compiled (:status compiled)))\\n  3977\\t        (is (<= 2 (count wrappers)) \\\"precondition: at least two stamped sites\\\")\\n  3978\\t        (is (some? k))\\n  3979\\t        (is (= :cc3-duplicate-stamp-site\\n  3980\\t               (try (cc3-oracle-binding (assoc compiled :ast duplicated))\\n  3981\\t                    ::no-failure\\n  3982\\t                    (catch Exception e (:rule (ex-data e)))))\\n  3983\\t            \\\"two wrappers carrying one site id refuse, never overwrite\\\")))))\\n  3984\\t\\n  3985\\t\\n  3986\\t(deftest test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins\\n  3987\\t  ;; cc3 r3 item F2: the admission coordinate is an explicit,\\n  3988\\t  ;; composition-supplied scope plus a per-scope ordinal, retained\\n  3989\\t  ;; with the compilation as plain data — no per-JVM global counter.\\n  3990\\t  ;; Two scopes whose ordinals both restarted at 0, admitting\\n  3991\\t  ;; identical content, mint distinct origins; replaying one retained\\n  3992\\t  ;; admission (the binding test above) keeps its one origin.\\n  3993\\t  (let [fixture {:id :cc3-binding\\n  3994\\t                 :call '(latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}\\n  3995\\t        a (kernel-compile fixture \\\"run-a\\\" 0)\\n  3996\\t        b (kernel-compile fixture \\\"run-b\\\" 0)]\\n  3997\\t    (is (= :compiled (:status a)))\\n  3998\\t    (is (= :compiled (:status b)))\\n  3999\\t    (is (= (:canonical-source-hash a) (:canonical-source-hash b))\\n  4000\\t        \\\"precondition: the content really is identical\\\")\\n  4001\\t    (is (= 0 (nth (:admission-origin a) 3) (nth (:admission-origin b) 3))\\n  4002\\t        \\\"precondition: both scopes restarted their ordinal at 0\\\")\\n  4003\\t    (is (= \\\"run-a\\\" (nth (:admission-origin a) 2)))\\n  4004\\t    (is (= \\\"run-b\\\" (nth (:admission-origin b) 2)))\\n  4005\\t    (is (not= (:admission-origin a) (:admission-origin b))\\n  4006\\t        \\\"distinct scopes with restarted ordinals mint distinct origins\\\")\\n  4007\\t    (let [ba (cc3-oracle-binding a)\\n  4008\\t          bb (cc3-oracle-binding b)]\\n  4009\\t      (is (= (:admission-origin a) (:origin ba)))\\n  4010\\t      (is (= (:admission-origin b) (:origin bb)))\\n  4011\\t      (is (= (:binding ba) (:binding (cc3-oracle-binding a)))\\n  4012\\t          \\\"replay reuses the recorded coordinate of scope run-a\\\")\\n  4013\\t      (is (= (set (keys (:binding ba))) (set (keys (:binding bb)))))\\n  4014\\t      (is (not= (set (vals (:binding ba))) (set (vals (:binding bb))))\\n  4015\\t          \\\"the same sites bind under each admission's own origin\\\"))))\\n   113\\tmeasurement method. It stands in the r1 findings as an\\n   114\\tincomplete-preflight run; nothing here re-stamps it. The r2 record\\n   115\\tadded serialized sizes, timings, and finite ceilings, but its\\n   116\\t\\\"retained memory\\\" figure was the canonical serialized byte count and\\n   117\\tits heap figure one post-binding sample; r3 replaces those two\\n   118\\tclaims with the measurements below and preserves the rest.\\n   119\\t\\n   120\\tMeasured 2026-11-11 in-session (JVM, warm; fixture\\n   121\\t`{:call (latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}` through\\n   122\\t`kernel-compile`, `cc3-oracle-binding`, `linearize/project-rows`,\\n   123\\t`derive/stack-image`, `derive/register-image`, and both tagged C\\n   124\\tlanes; script `/tmp/cc3-f6-measure.clj`):\\n   125\\t\\n   126\\t- Serialized storage: canonical byte counts (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`)\\n   127\\t  of the C1 rows and of the 3-lane provenance relation. This measures\\n   128\\t  storage bytes, not live objects.\\n   129\\t- Retained JVM memory: used-heap delta (`Runtime.totalMemory −\\n   130\\t  freeMemory`) around the retained structure's lifetime\\n   131\\t  (`{binding, semantic/stack/register images, relation}` held in a\\n   132\\t  holder), with `System/gc()` pins before each sample, repeated for\\n   133\\t  stability. Method limits: process-wide JVM figure including the\\n   134\\t  test harness; `System/gc()` is a hint the JVM honored observably\\n   135\\t  here, not a guarantee; the delta is comparable only on this\\n   136\\t  host/JVM and only as an order-of-magnitude retained-size claim,\\n   137\\t  never as an exact object-graph size.\\n   138\\t- Peak memory: a sampler thread recorded used heap every 5 ms across\\n   139\\t  lowering → persistence (binding/projection/derives) → tagged\\n   140\\t  execution (both C lanes); the peak is the maximum sample, checked\\n   141\\t  against the declared ceiling. Boundary samples per stage are also\\n   142\\t  recorded. Limit: 5 ms sampling can miss sub-5 ms transients.\\n   143\\t\\n   144\\tF6-NUMBERS-TBD\\n   145\\t\\n   146\\tFailure rule (unchanged): exceeding any ceiling is a failed bounded\\n   147\\trun; bounds are never silently raised.\\n   148\\t\\n   149\\t## Red-first evidence\\n   150\\t\\n   151\\tTests were written before the fix for each item; observed red in this\\n   152\\tsession:\\n   153\\t\\n   154\\t| Item | Red | Green |\\n   155\\t|---|---|---|\\n   156\\t| F1+F2 (oracle) | `test-cc3-correspondence-verifies-grammar-data` + `test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins`: 7 failures, 1 error (scalar mutations accepted, non-`gate-site!` wrapper accepted, duplicate IDs silently overwritten; distinct test errored on the not-yet-existing scoped arity) | 0 (both tests, plus nested + binding deftests: 4 tests, 64 assertions) |\\n   157\\t| F4 (durable) | `repl-packet-provenance-survives-failure-test`: 2 failures (throwing round added no handle — 2 handles before and after; no retrievable relation for the throwing round) | 0 (7 assertions; with the r2 durable test: 2 tests, 14 assertions) |\\n   158\\t| F6 | n/a — record/measurement fix, no code | measured record above |\\n   159\\t\\n   160\\t## Verification\\n   161\\t\\n   162\\t| Lane | Command | Outcome |\\n   163\\t|---|---|---|\\n   164\\t| Callsite battery | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 35 tests, 396 assertio