while preserving the failed run ([design:329](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:329)); shrinking the fixture is therefore not mandatory.\\n\\nBefore fresh tagged evidence, the new declaration must state:\\n\\n- The pinned corpus/revision, host/JVM settings, retained object set—including compiled input and reconstruction evidence—and maximum simultaneously retained fixtures.\\n- Separate finite storage, retained-memory, peak-heap, and time ceilings, justified by the pilot measurements with explicit headroom.\\n- The exact reproducible measurement procedure, including the compiled-inclusive variant, repetitions, sampling limitations, and maximum-based pass/fail rule.\\n- The superseded run’s failed status and exceedances, without relabelling it successful.\\n\\nF1/F3/F5 remain confirmed within their previously stated scope.\\n\\nCONFIRMATION VERDICT: REQUEST CHANGES\"}}\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794202500000-architect-cc1-recheck-r2.findings.md:43:   Jing encodes vector metadata: [cbor.cljc:904](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:904) calls `meta-bytes`; [cbor.cljc:834](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:834) removes only reader-position keys, leaving `::origin-of`. Encoding its function value reaches the unsupported-value refusal. The bounded runner converts the exception into `:body-error` at [macro.cljc:829](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:829).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-engineer-cc3-fix-r5.prompt.md:6:# Task: cc3 fix round r5 — F2 caller threading, F6 median defect, and the NEW VERSIONED BOUNDED RUN per astra's ruling (c)\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-engineer-cc3-fix-r5.prompt.md:15:Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3`, branch `cc3-lowering-provenance`, base `ced