cc3-fix-r8.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:12:**Red first.** `/tmp/cc3-r8-red.clj`: a store refusing only provenance writes (payload-keyed on `:yin.vm.provenance/schema` / `:yin.repl.call-provenance/schema`) produced `t3=\"42\"`, `handles=nil`, `observable? false` for both relation and record writes — the r7 blanket catch swallowed the only signal. After the fix the same probe prints `42\\nWarning: this round's call provenance was not retained (relation write failed: store refused the provenance write); the program's value is unaffected` (resp. `record write failed: …`), `observable? true`.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794405917000-engineer-cc3-fix-r8.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:17:- `run-evaluator-stage`'s `retaining-load` records, for a **claimed** admission only, `{:admission :root :stage :message}` into a failures volatile. No handle is assoc'd for a failed packet; completed handles in the same round still merge as before. An unclaimed packet (no entry in `:call-site-round-claims`) or a nil retention (no store / no claim) records nothing — failed retention is distinguished from an unclaimed admission.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794405917000-engineer-cc3-fix-r8.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:18:- Failures ride the session state as `:call-provenance-failures` (public accessor `yin.repl/call-provenance-failures`) beside `:call-provenance-handles`, and the round's slice as `:call-provenance-round-failures`, which `with-index-notice` renders as a second Warning line (`retention-notice`: `Warning: this round's call provenance was not retained (relation write failed: <msg>); the program's value is unaffected`) and consumes. This is the observable surface that works when indexing succeeded and the indexer (`index.cljc:549`, indexer state only, running before retention) has nothing to report. The Warning text is additive only — existing index/query contracts (`3\\nWarning: … materialize failed …`) still pass unmodified; no test contract was changed.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794405917000-engineer-cc3-fix-r8.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:25:- `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` `repl-retention-failure-is-observable-test`: healthy defs first (handles present), then the store starts refusing only provenance writes; `(g)` still answers `42`, the Warning names the failed stage, exactly one admission-scoped failure with the right `:stage` is recorded, handles equal the earlier set (no incomplete handle, earlier survive), and an unclaimed literal round adds no failure and no Warning.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794405917000-engineer-cc3-fix-r8.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:42:Note: one intermediate assertion (repeat `(g)` is unclaimed) failed on first run — each round mints a fresh admission, so a repeat call *is* claimed; the test now uses an unclaimed literal round instead. Contract change stated above: none to existing tests; the only new surface is the additive Warning line, `call-provenance-failures`, and `:call-provenance-failures` on session state.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794407164000-engineer-cc3-fix-r9.prompt.md:11:- Status-Event: 2026-11-12 09:5x +0700 | Model: muse-wonder-1.0 | Status: failed | Rationale: provider 429, quota window resets 2026-11-16T00:00Z (weekly boundary); zero work done\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-engineer-cc3-fix-r5.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:7:# cc3 fix round r5 — F2 caller threading, F6 maximum rule, bounded run v2: findings\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-engineer-cc3-fix-r5.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:17:(`collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md`).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-engineer-cc3-fix-r5.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:81:  The superseded run stays FAILED — see the v2 declaration §5.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojur